  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_crest_cb22cb503b9597111b7b4afa50dba4883e57ff655dac77486b4d4b2c80e4e45062">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>crest, a measure of linen cloth (OED s.v. crest n.3) | a measure of Britanny cloth (5 ells) (TNA: PRO, E159/177 Recorda Michaelmas m 5) | linen cloth from Britanny, so called because measured in crests (= 5 ells) (OED s.v. crest n.^3) | linen cloth from Britanny, so called because measured in crests (= 5 ells) (OED s.v. crest n.3) | a crest is a measure of Britanny cloth (5 ells) (TNA: PRO, E159/177 Recorda Michaelmas m 5), so crest cloth is presumably cloth manufactured in Britanny and therefore measured in crests. However, the account states that one piece measuring 100 ulne was imported | a crest is a measure of Britanny cloth (5 ells) (TNA: PRO, E159/177 Recorda Michaelmas m 5), so crest cloth is presumably cloth manufactured in Britanny and therefore measured in crests | linen cloth from Britanny, so called because measured in crests (= 5 ells) (OED s.v. crest n.3) | linen cloth from Brittany, so called because measured in crests (= 5 ells) (OED s.v. crest n.3)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
